WEBVTT

00:08.180 --> 00:09.380
Wait! Wait!

00:09.380 --> 00:10.740
Wait up!

00:11.600 --> 00:12.920
Wait, Joule!

00:12.920 --> 00:14.500
Wait! Wait!

00:16.080 --> 00:17.980
Wait, Feat!

00:28.170 --> 00:30.120
What're you doing, Alan?

00:30.800 --> 00:32.620
I'm teaching Joule!

00:33.510 --> 00:35.770
We want to talk to Feat and the other beasts!

00:37.220 --> 00:40.920
Oh! I bet it'd be a lot 
of fun if we could, huh?

00:54.360 --> 01:00.660
<b>A Journey Through Another World: 
Raising Kids While Adventuring</b>

02:16.490 --> 02:21.490
<b>We're Gonna Beat the Goblins!</b>

02:19.220 --> 02:24.370
One, two, three, four...

02:22.990 --> 02:27.000
<b>Day 1</b>

02:24.370 --> 02:29.420
Five, six, seven, eight...

02:29.720 --> 02:30.950
Nine...

02:30.950 --> 02:31.630
Ten!

02:32.010 --> 02:34.480
That's right. Good job.

02:34.480 --> 02:36.520
This is one copper coin.

02:36.520 --> 02:38.590
What do ten of these make?

02:39.990 --> 02:41.300
Um...

02:41.640 --> 02:42.390
This!

02:42.390 --> 02:44.910
Yes! One large copper.

02:44.910 --> 02:47.100
And what do ten large coppers make?

02:47.450 --> 02:48.790
Um...

02:48.790 --> 02:49.440
This?

02:49.440 --> 02:51.560
You got it! One silver.

02:51.910 --> 02:53.900
Want to try a harder one now?

02:54.240 --> 02:55.230
Yeah!

02:55.650 --> 02:58.690
Okay, let's make 54 gold.

02:59.200 --> 03:01.910
Let's see... This big one is...

03:02.400 --> 03:06.990
One, two, three, four, five!

03:07.570 --> 03:08.830
And the little one...

03:09.330 --> 03:13.170
One, two, three, four!

03:13.390 --> 03:14.400
Correct!

03:14.400 --> 03:15.380
What's next?

03:15.380 --> 03:17.130
Wow, you guys sure are motivated.

03:17.470 --> 03:20.550
Okay, this is a ten-gold appe fruit,

03:20.550 --> 03:23.590
and this is a sixteen-gold oren fruit.

03:24.050 --> 03:27.420
How much would it cost to buy one of each?

03:35.910 --> 03:37.270
Twenty-six gold!

03:37.270 --> 03:38.560
Correct!

03:38.560 --> 03:41.110
Okay, let's go to town and do some shopping.

03:41.450 --> 03:43.070
Yay!

03:49.300 --> 03:50.700
A few for your home?

03:50.700 --> 03:52.410
Only the freshest here!

03:55.760 --> 03:56.590
Welcome.

03:56.900 --> 03:58.550
We're here to shop!

03:58.880 --> 04:01.760
Well, thank you. 
Take your time choosing, okay?

04:08.940 --> 04:10.140
Did you decide what you want?

04:10.830 --> 04:12.250
Yep!

04:12.250 --> 04:15.640
Okay, Alan, you go first. 
Remember to say "please."

04:15.640 --> 04:16.060
Okay!

04:16.490 --> 04:18.150
I want this, please!

04:18.390 --> 04:20.360
All right, sherry fruit for you.

04:20.360 --> 04:21.610
How many would you like?

04:21.840 --> 04:23.260
Um...

04:24.460 --> 04:25.200
Five!

04:25.200 --> 04:28.780
Five, eh? That'll be 35 gold.

04:29.200 --> 04:31.750
Um, let me see...

04:32.000 --> 04:33.080
Here!

04:33.410 --> 04:35.790
Oh, that's exactly right! Very good!

04:36.290 --> 04:38.470
Good job!

04:38.470 --> 04:39.500
You're next, Elena.

04:40.110 --> 04:41.960
I want this, please!

04:42.490 --> 04:45.430
Appe fruit? Okay. How many?

04:45.850 --> 04:46.760
Five!

04:47.000 --> 04:49.470
That'll be thirty gold.

04:49.740 --> 04:51.290
Okay, um...

04:51.730 --> 04:52.310
Here!

04:52.690 --> 04:54.250
Exact change. Perfect.

04:54.250 --> 04:55.020
Thank you!

04:55.390 --> 04:56.980
We did it!

04:57.320 --> 05:01.900
They count money so well 
for such young children.

05:01.900 --> 05:04.400
You must be doing a great job raising them.

05:04.950 --> 05:07.910
Oh... Thank you.

05:08.390 --> 05:10.100
Bye-bye!

05:11.440 --> 05:12.480
Inventory.

05:17.540 --> 05:20.380
I'd like to go to the bookstore 
next. Is that okay?

05:20.870 --> 05:22.340
Let's go!

05:25.060 --> 05:26.520
So many books!

05:26.520 --> 05:29.260
That's right. There are lots of them.

05:31.810 --> 05:34.880
<i>Since I've acquired water magic skills,</i>

05:34.880 --> 05:36.880
<i>I need to learn how to use them.</i>

05:42.480 --> 05:45.320
What you see written here are letters.

05:45.320 --> 05:46.200
Letters?

05:46.460 --> 05:47.600
That's right.

05:47.600 --> 05:50.780
Would you two like to learn 
how to read letters, too?

05:50.780 --> 05:51.990
Yes!

05:53.840 --> 05:55.450
What energetic children.

05:55.820 --> 06:00.650
I have some reading practice 
textbooks and simple picture books.

06:00.650 --> 06:01.790
How about it?

06:02.060 --> 06:03.430
Thank you very much.

06:03.500 --> 06:05.420
Thank you very much.

06:05.420 --> 06:06.760
Oh, what good kids!

06:07.170 --> 06:09.110
Was it you who taught them that?

06:09.110 --> 06:10.470
Well, yes.

06:10.770 --> 06:13.060
That's impressive for a young man like you.

06:13.810 --> 06:15.490
Thank you.

06:16.590 --> 06:20.900
<i>It made me kind of happy hearing so 
much praise from the people in town.</i>

06:21.870 --> 06:28.000
<i>It sort of reassured me that I'd been 
interacting with Alan and Elena properly.</i>

06:28.570 --> 06:31.030
<b>Day 2</b>

06:31.440 --> 06:35.490
<i>The next day, we went to the guild and 
accepted our first quest in a while.</i>

06:36.130 --> 06:39.530
<i>It was a quest to find a missing cat.</i>

06:40.890 --> 06:43.160
Your time limit is two days.

06:43.160 --> 06:44.800
Try your best!

06:44.800 --> 06:46.760
'Kay!

06:50.030 --> 06:52.380
It's a black cat with white paws.

06:52.380 --> 06:53.680
Its name is Mina.

06:54.180 --> 06:55.640
Mina!

06:57.700 --> 06:59.600
It went missing somewhere around here.

07:04.570 --> 07:05.660
Joule!

07:05.660 --> 07:06.960
Feat!

07:06.960 --> 07:07.860
Bolt!

07:08.190 --> 07:10.070
Will you guys help us out?

07:13.380 --> 07:14.870
Mina?

07:15.200 --> 07:16.330
Mina?

07:16.610 --> 07:17.790
Mina?

07:26.800 --> 07:28.340
Mina?

07:31.950 --> 07:32.720
Wrong one.

07:34.650 --> 07:35.640
Mina?

07:36.700 --> 07:38.100
Huh?

07:40.010 --> 07:41.360
Mina?

07:42.800 --> 07:44.220
Nope.

07:46.800 --> 07:48.550
Not Mina...

07:48.990 --> 07:50.990
Okay, let's look over there next.

07:51.980 --> 07:53.110
Mina?

07:53.750 --> 07:54.860
Mina?

07:55.290 --> 07:56.410
Mina?

07:57.040 --> 07:58.700
Mina?

08:00.710 --> 08:02.410
No Mina.

08:02.770 --> 08:05.110
What do you think? Should we stop looking?

08:05.110 --> 08:06.180
No!

08:06.180 --> 08:07.510
We'll look!

08:07.510 --> 08:09.380
Okay. Let's keep at it, then.

08:09.750 --> 08:11.680
Which way should we go next?

08:11.680 --> 08:13.090
That way!

08:25.680 --> 08:26.270
Is that...

08:26.680 --> 08:27.700
Mina!

08:27.700 --> 08:28.480
There you are!

08:29.150 --> 08:31.440
She'll get scared if we approach too quickly.

08:31.440 --> 08:32.880
Go slowly, okay?

08:32.880 --> 08:33.700
Okay.

08:36.160 --> 08:38.120
Quietly...

08:41.350 --> 08:44.290
Quietly...

08:44.690 --> 08:46.010
Mina.

08:46.010 --> 08:47.870
Don't be scared.

08:54.630 --> 08:56.000
Mina.

08:56.000 --> 08:57.220
Come here.

08:57.440 --> 08:58.520
Mina.

08:58.590 --> 08:59.980
Mina.

09:04.380 --> 09:06.100
We did it!

09:07.180 --> 09:10.570
Yep, the name on the collar 
matches. It's Mina.

09:12.630 --> 09:14.660
I wonder if she's hungry.

09:14.660 --> 09:16.130
Let's get food, Taku!

09:16.130 --> 09:17.280
Food! Food!

09:17.280 --> 09:19.490
Okay, okay. How about milk?

09:20.910 --> 09:22.330
Orc Meat

09:20.910 --> 09:22.330
Milk

09:20.910 --> 09:22.330
Honey

09:31.670 --> 09:32.880
She's drinking!

09:34.360 --> 09:36.340
I'm so glad!

09:39.020 --> 09:44.020
<i>And then we returned Mina to her 
owner, who was waiting at the guild.</i>

09:44.020 --> 09:47.020
Thank you so, so much!

09:47.020 --> 09:49.780
Come on, let's go home, Mina.

09:51.020 --> 09:52.650
Well, ready to go home?

09:52.650 --> 09:53.730
No!

09:53.730 --> 09:55.440
I want to search more!

09:55.440 --> 09:56.430
Me, too!

09:56.430 --> 09:58.300
We wanna search!

09:58.300 --> 10:01.710
I'm sorry. Do you have any other quests?

10:01.710 --> 10:02.700
Well...

10:03.130 --> 10:06.160
It's not a search quest, 
but I do have one other,

10:06.770 --> 10:08.620
though it's not exactly for children...

10:09.690 --> 10:11.900
Killing goblins, huh?

10:11.900 --> 10:15.170
Yes. Goblins showed up 
at the next village over,

10:15.170 --> 10:17.590
and they've been harming 
people and livestock.

10:18.250 --> 10:21.030
It's a bit much for low-ranked adventurers,

10:21.030 --> 10:26.400
but the reward isn't great, so mid-range 
adventurers don't want to do it.

10:26.400 --> 10:27.560
I see.

10:27.850 --> 10:30.520
What do you think? 
Want to take out some goblins?

10:30.520 --> 10:33.480
<b>Goblins</b>

10:31.290 --> 10:32.710
Goblins?

10:32.710 --> 10:33.480
Are they yummy?

10:33.730 --> 10:36.940
I-If I had to guess, I'd say 
they probably aren't, no.

10:41.870 --> 10:43.680
So fast!

10:48.290 --> 10:51.750
Thanks, Joule. Could you go 
back to your small form now?

10:55.200 --> 10:56.460
You too, Feat.

11:00.200 --> 11:01.900
Bolt, thanks for your help, too.

11:03.680 --> 11:05.560
Okay, lets head into the village.

11:06.020 --> 11:07.020
Who are you?!

11:07.380 --> 11:11.960
We're adventurers who accepted your 
quest in Shireen to kill the goblins.

11:11.960 --> 11:12.980
Adventurers?

11:12.980 --> 11:16.190
Yes. I'd like to meet with the village chief.

11:17.950 --> 11:19.900
Understood. I'll show you the way.

11:23.490 --> 11:26.010
You're really on high alert, huh?

11:26.010 --> 11:28.830
The goblins have been attacking 
several times a day.

11:29.080 --> 11:31.290
That often?

11:32.390 --> 11:36.250
Thank you for accepting this quest.

11:36.600 --> 11:38.960
I'm the head of this village.

11:39.320 --> 11:44.180
If we can get right to the point, 
can you tell me about these goblins?

11:44.530 --> 11:45.680
Yes.

11:45.680 --> 11:49.270
Incidentally, will your companions 
be joining you later?

11:49.270 --> 11:51.730
Huh? No, it's just us three.

11:52.060 --> 11:54.940
Er... Are you sure you can handle it?

11:55.320 --> 11:58.650
<i>Ah... I guess we don't 
look that strong, do we?</i>

11:58.990 --> 12:00.960
This should tell you what you need to know.

12:00.960 --> 12:02.110
A-rank?!

12:02.530 --> 12:05.980
Yes. Goblin slaying is 
well within our abilities.

12:05.980 --> 12:07.520
You needn't worry.

12:07.520 --> 12:10.680
P-Please accept my apologies!

12:12.120 --> 12:13.330
Ch-Chief!

12:13.330 --> 12:14.790
Goblins in the village!

12:15.720 --> 12:18.590
I'll get rid of them. 
All of you, stay where it's safe.

12:19.940 --> 12:22.010
You're taking the children with you?

12:22.400 --> 12:26.480
It's easier to protect them 
if they're within sight

12:26.480 --> 12:28.010
than if I just leave them wherever.

12:28.510 --> 12:30.670
<i>Let's... just leave it at that.</i>

12:43.200 --> 12:44.570
Air Shot!

12:46.070 --> 12:48.120
Are you all right? Can you stand?

12:48.120 --> 12:50.700
Y-Yes. Thank you.

12:51.230 --> 12:54.660
We'll handle things here! Get away, quickly!

12:55.040 --> 12:56.250
Can we beat them?

12:56.590 --> 12:58.920
You can, but be careful.

12:59.510 --> 13:00.170
Okay!

13:06.870 --> 13:11.060
You guys too? Okay, but Joule 
and Feat, stay in those forms.

13:11.060 --> 13:12.650
No getting big, okay?

13:28.010 --> 13:30.920
<i>That one's bigger than the others.</i>

13:30.920 --> 13:31.660
<i>Appraise.</i>

13:32.160 --> 13:33.540
<i>Goblin Soldier...</i>

13:34.320 --> 13:36.060
<i>A high-rank variant of goblin.</i>

13:37.230 --> 13:38.380
<i>I'll take that one—</i>

13:43.910 --> 13:45.920
All done!

13:46.530 --> 13:48.920
<i>I didn't even get a turn...</i>

13:50.710 --> 13:52.720
You beat <i>all</i> the goblins?

13:52.970 --> 13:53.970
Yep! We—

13:53.970 --> 13:55.090
<i>We did!</i>

13:57.190 --> 13:59.400
Huh? Was that voice...

13:59.680 --> 14:01.010
Joule?

14:01.010 --> 14:02.670
<i>Yep, it was me!</i>

14:03.870 --> 14:06.740
Oh, Telepathy? When did you learn that?

14:06.740 --> 14:09.570
<i>I was able to use it 
after I beat the goblins.</i>

14:10.010 --> 14:14.540
<i>I knew he was male, but I guess he's 
a lot younger than I thought...</i>

14:14.890 --> 14:18.000
<i>Now I can talk with all of you, Master!</i>

14:18.350 --> 14:21.860
Um, could you not call me "Master"?

14:21.860 --> 14:24.210
<i>Why? I can't call you "Master"?</i>

14:24.560 --> 14:28.430
It's not that... I'm just not 
used to it, and it feels weird.

14:28.430 --> 14:29.550
"Takumi" is fine.

14:31.130 --> 14:34.560
You don't like that? 
Okay, anything but "Master," then.

14:34.560 --> 14:35.810
How about "Taku"?

14:35.810 --> 14:37.230
That's what we call him.

14:37.230 --> 14:39.010
<i>Okay! Taku!</i>

14:39.010 --> 14:41.010
<i>Can I call you "Taku"?</i>

14:41.010 --> 14:41.980
Sure, that's fine.

14:42.370 --> 14:45.760
<i>Then can I call you "Mister Taku"?</i>

14:45.760 --> 14:47.900
<i>Please allow me to call you "Chief."</i>

14:47.900 --> 14:49.110
Feat!

14:49.110 --> 14:49.860
Bolt!

14:50.150 --> 14:51.290
You guys, too?

14:51.290 --> 14:53.330
<i>Yep! We learned Telepathy!</i>

14:53.690 --> 14:55.920
<i>I suspected Feat was female.</i>

14:55.920 --> 14:58.050
<i>Sounds like I was right.</i>

14:58.050 --> 14:59.610
<i>And Bolt...</i>

14:59.610 --> 15:01.760
Bolt, you're a male, right?

15:01.760 --> 15:05.920
<i>Yes. I'm very fond of the name 
"Bolt." It's quite manly.</i>

15:05.920 --> 15:08.300
Really? Glad to hear it.

15:09.300 --> 15:12.960
<i>Alan and Elena, I hope we'll 
be even better friends!</i>

15:12.960 --> 15:13.850
<i>Me, too!</i>

15:14.280 --> 15:15.810
<i>I look forward to our continued friendship.</i>

15:16.100 --> 15:16.770
Yeah!

15:17.370 --> 15:19.260
I taught them words!

15:19.260 --> 15:20.730
Now we can talk to them!

15:21.080 --> 15:24.690
<i>Oh, that's right. 
They did do that, didn't they?</i>

15:31.650 --> 15:34.620
That's amazing. You did great.

15:37.460 --> 15:38.800
<i>Mister Taku!</i>

15:37.460 --> 15:38.800
<i>Taku!</i>

15:38.800 --> 15:40.790
<i>Me, too! Me, too!</i>

15:39.450 --> 15:40.790
<i>Me, too!</i>

15:41.260 --> 15:42.250
Okay, okay.

15:42.800 --> 15:44.210
You're very clever.

15:49.600 --> 15:50.620
What's that?

15:50.620 --> 15:51.720
<i>I'll go take a look!</i>

15:52.680 --> 15:54.960
Did the goblins set it on fire?

15:54.960 --> 15:58.060
Okay, I guess it's time to 
test out my water magic.

15:58.710 --> 16:03.060
<i>I read </i>The Basics of Magic<i> last 
night, so I know how to use it.</i>

16:08.180 --> 16:09.630
<i>Gather, water!</i>

16:12.380 --> 16:13.530
Water Ball!

16:17.790 --> 16:19.540
Huh? That's weird...

16:20.290 --> 16:21.700
<i>Gather, water!</i>

16:24.570 --> 16:25.670
Water Ball!

16:27.130 --> 16:29.020
Huh? Wait, why?!

16:29.020 --> 16:30.590
Do I not have enough magic?

16:30.990 --> 16:32.720
Okay, one more try!

16:34.480 --> 16:35.890
Gather, water!

16:35.890 --> 16:38.470
Water Ball!

16:43.600 --> 16:45.400
Joule, throw some water on it.

16:45.840 --> 16:46.990
<i>Got it!</i>

16:53.660 --> 16:57.430
<i>I'd better read </i>The Basics of 
Magic<i> again when we get home.</i>

17:03.850 --> 17:05.730
<i>They're comforting me...</i>

17:08.140 --> 17:09.370
Thank you!

17:12.000 --> 17:14.030
<i>After we successfully got 
rid of the goblins...</i>

17:14.030 --> 17:15.510
Good work!

17:15.820 --> 17:20.770
<i>...we left the village, collected our 
reward at the guild, and went home.</i>

17:20.770 --> 17:23.640
<i>Between searching for a lost 
cat and slaying goblins,</i>

17:23.640 --> 17:26.430
<i>Alan and Elena were on the move all day.</i>

17:26.430 --> 17:28.000
<i>I thought they'd be tired out, but...</i>

17:28.000 --> 17:29.360
Taku!

17:29.770 --> 17:31.070
Read us a picture book!

17:31.400 --> 17:33.640
<i>I was way off.</i>

17:34.160 --> 17:35.530
Sure.

17:37.850 --> 17:40.500
"There are lots of fish in the ocean."

17:41.390 --> 17:42.200
Ocean?

17:42.200 --> 17:42.950
Fish?

17:43.310 --> 17:47.420
Oh, right. You two haven't 
seen the ocean yet, have you?

17:49.400 --> 17:50.410
The ocean, huh?

17:52.250 --> 17:55.220
<b>Day 3</b>

17:52.860 --> 17:55.220
You're leaving Shireen?!

17:55.640 --> 17:59.300
I wondered what was going on when you 
called us here so early in the morning.

17:59.300 --> 18:03.540
Sorry. Any other time,
I would have gone to you myself.

18:03.540 --> 18:06.180
We don't mind that, but what brought this on?

18:06.610 --> 18:10.900
I wanted to show the kids more of the world.

18:11.180 --> 18:13.110
Have you decided where you'll be going?

18:13.390 --> 18:17.320
I'm thinking we'll head south 
to the seaside town of Bailey.

18:17.710 --> 18:20.280
Bailey, eh? That's within the kingdom.

18:22.790 --> 18:27.710
You were too visibly relieved to learn that 
they would still be within the kingdom.

18:28.140 --> 18:31.280
There's not much chance of war 
breaking out at the moment,

18:31.280 --> 18:34.180
but a monster uprising 
could happen at any time.

18:35.280 --> 18:39.680
And we don't want Takumi's strength 
ending up on the enemy's side.

18:40.110 --> 18:42.220
Not the kids, either.

18:42.550 --> 18:45.160
I just never get tired of watching them.

18:45.160 --> 18:48.190
I always feel like they're 
gonna do something wild!

18:48.190 --> 18:50.030
I do agree with that.

18:51.190 --> 18:54.150
<i>The next day, before leaving town,</i>

18:54.460 --> 18:57.110
<i>we visited all the folks 
who had been there for us.</i>

18:57.570 --> 18:58.320
What?!

18:58.700 --> 19:01.130
You're leaving town, Takumi?

19:01.130 --> 19:02.280
Y-Yes...

19:02.610 --> 19:05.240
But you'll come back, right?

19:05.490 --> 19:08.450
Huh? Luna, are you actually in...

19:09.010 --> 19:11.540
With all kinds of rare materials!

19:11.540 --> 19:12.420
Of course...

19:12.980 --> 19:15.380
I see. Going on a journey, eh?

19:15.670 --> 19:18.100
You are adventurers, after all.

19:18.100 --> 19:20.340
It'll feel a bit lonely here without you,

19:20.750 --> 19:22.540
but traveling sounds like fun!

19:22.540 --> 19:23.210
Yeah!

19:23.210 --> 19:24.750
We'll see you again!

19:24.750 --> 19:26.310
So, anyway, there's a favor I wanted to ask.

19:26.910 --> 19:30.410
Could you make enough 
bread to last us a while?

19:30.410 --> 19:31.980
Sure! You can count on us!

19:31.980 --> 19:33.520
So what kind would you like?

19:33.900 --> 19:35.910
Cream bread, red bean buns,

19:35.910 --> 19:39.240
and some kukuru bread made 
with these kukuru nuts.

19:39.690 --> 19:42.520
Ah, kukuru nuts, eh?

19:42.520 --> 19:43.160
Oh, and...

19:43.440 --> 19:46.240
I'd like you to make sliced 
bread using this pan.

19:46.760 --> 19:49.580
I don't know where you keep 
pulling all these ideas from...

19:49.890 --> 19:51.080
Red bean buns!

19:51.080 --> 19:52.540
Cream bread!

19:53.430 --> 19:55.250
Oh, welcome!

19:57.840 --> 19:59.380
Summer clothes!

19:59.380 --> 20:01.720
Oh, gosh! You look so cute!

20:02.990 --> 20:04.940
Um, how much for these?

20:04.940 --> 20:06.880
Don't you worry about that.

20:06.880 --> 20:10.390
Think of it as a goodbye 
gift from me. They're yours.

20:10.960 --> 20:12.620
<i>And finally...</i>

20:13.660 --> 20:14.770
Boo!

20:16.760 --> 20:17.320
Boo!

20:25.190 --> 20:26.050
<i>Syl.</i>

20:32.390 --> 20:33.470
Takumi...

20:34.220 --> 20:36.460
Takumi! Have you been well?

20:37.850 --> 20:38.750
Taku?

20:39.180 --> 20:41.210
Uh, I'm fine. Don't worry.

20:41.630 --> 20:44.140
Syl, don't scare me like that!

20:44.140 --> 20:46.110
I-I'm sorry...

20:46.110 --> 20:47.050
And don't cry.

20:47.320 --> 20:50.480
But you haven't come to 
visit me lately at all!

20:50.480 --> 20:51.520
<i>That's</i> why?

20:52.040 --> 20:53.680
The thing is, Syl,

20:53.680 --> 20:56.940
we've decided to leave 
Shireen and head to Bailey.

20:57.180 --> 20:59.220
What? You have?

20:59.220 --> 21:01.900
I wanted to show those two the ocean.

21:02.300 --> 21:05.970
The ocean... Well, it has 
gotten warmer, after all.

21:05.970 --> 21:07.270
That sounds nice!

21:07.270 --> 21:10.160
I'll be in touch once we get to Bailey.

21:10.560 --> 21:14.710
I should just talk to a statue in one 
of your shrines, like I do here, right?

21:14.710 --> 21:16.620
Yes! I'll be waiting!

21:17.710 --> 21:22.130
Alan, Elena, we'll be saying 
goodbye to this city for a while.

21:22.420 --> 21:24.470
Goodbye!

21:28.790 --> 21:30.930
Hold it! Those kids...

21:31.760 --> 21:34.900
Those kids are my merchandise!

21:34.900 --> 21:36.270
Give them back to me!

21:40.710 --> 21:42.400
Monsters! A lot of them!

21:43.020 --> 21:45.200
Throw this one out as bait while we flee!

21:45.200 --> 21:46.110
No!

21:46.420 --> 21:48.000
Let go, you brat!

21:48.000 --> 21:49.280
Hurry! They're catching up!

21:49.820 --> 21:52.240
There! You can both go!

22:06.480 --> 22:08.630
Alan... Elena...

23:45.020 --> 23:50.030
<b>Next Time</b>

23:45.520 --> 23:50.030
<b>The Ocean! It's Salty!</b>

23:45.920 --> 23:47.030
The Ocean!

23:47.030 --> 23:49.200
It's Salty!
